Engine: the window hidden only when the starter asks, and shown again on request (open fix 43).

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written and proved by work order 185 (Part 2),
parked for Data (doc/briefs/185-parked-for-data.md). No engine patch may
be applied in that order. It AMENDS open fix 41 (applied, 4bf152e4): it
replaces 41's `g_hide_window = true` start and keeps 41's other half, a
hidden window presenting without VSync.

PROOF (work order 185, 27 September 2026): in a scratch worktree of
orionlayer-local 4bf152e4 with its own build directory (never on
orionlayer-local itself, never the build play.py starts) this file applied
with `patch -p1 --dry-run` and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz, and the
applied tree equals the scratch commit; the scratch engine was built in
full (Debug, ORION2RE_EXT=ON, as the linux-debug preset) — no error — every
changed .cpp compiles alone with the build's own command, and a control,
the same file with `MSG_SHOW_WINDOW` misspelt `MSG_SHOW_WINDW` in
ext_api.cpp, was refused by the compiler. The scratch engine then ran on
the virtual display: see the entry, doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 43.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch (after fix 41,
and after fix 42 if that is applied — they touch different files):

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_engine_window_on_request.patch

then rebuild, and set ORION2RE_HIDE_WINDOW=1 where OrionLayer starts the
engine (tools/vdisplay.engine_env). It comes back off with `patch -R -p1`
and a rebuild, which returns the engine to fix 41 as applied.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Fix 41 hides the window from the start, always: an ORION2RE_EXT engine
    started on its own is invisible and stays so, and nothing can show
    its window. With this patch the window is hidden at start only when
    the environment says ORION2RE_HIDE_WINDOW (non-empty, not "0") — what
    OrionLayer's start would set — and a client can show or hide it at any
    time with MSG_SHOW_WINDOW (0x86, one byte: 1 show, 0 hide), applied on
    the main thread, which owns the window. ext::Init no longer forces the
    flag on. One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 43.`, on one line at every
    changed place.

